From 7c92acbb5d194759b9fe31c4fc95403c623d3890 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well83 <well83@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:53:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: wireless: add ssv6x5x (iComm SV6256P / SSV6006C SDIO)
 for T95 H616

Some T95 H616 boards (e.g. AXP313A-V6.1) ship an iComm SV6256P SDIO
Wi-Fi chip (SDIO 0x3030:0x3030). Android already maps it to the
ssv6x5x module (libhwinfo, libwifi-hal-ssv, firmware in
hardware/ssv/wlan/firmware/ssv6x5x), only the kernel driver was missing.

Based on cdhigh/armbian_sv6256p 43c2ede2 (6.x port of the iComm vendor
driver; its ssv6x5x-sw.bin is byte-identical to the Android SDK one),
backported to 5.4:
- compat layer (include/ssv_compat.h): proc_ops/pde_data, vif->cfg,
  sta->deflink, beacon_get_tim/conf_tx link_id, bss_info_changed u32,
  wake_tx_queue, usb_driver drvwrap
- Allwinner glue: sunxi_wlan_set_power + sunxi_mmc_rescan_card (same
  sequence as the BSP ssv6158 driver) instead of the rockchip dummy
- original module parameter names (stacfgpath, cfgfirmwarepath,
  ssv_initmac) as passed by libhwinfo; default cfg path in /vendor
- fix SSV_AMPDU_SN_a_minus_b: nested macro self-initialised _a/_b
  (bug also in the iComm vendor code)
- uninitialised pointers in error paths, && vs & , min_t
- in-tree build: absolute KBUILD_TOP, no writes into the source tree

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
